  "note": "Election of one third (five seats), polled Friday 15 October 1937, for the five members elected in January 1933. Seven were nominated; Samuel Ewart withdrew. \"All the candidates nominated are Unionists\" (Belfast Telegraph). Lunn, Monroe, Malcomson and Hill were retiring members. Electorate 5,529; votes polled 2,227."
